      "nets": ["/NET0019", "/NET0009", "/NET0026", "/NET0027", "/NET0030", "/NET0032"],
      "observed": "R7 and R20 are both populated as 0 Ω and both connect to /NET0019; their other ends go to /NET0009 (J3/J9 pin 19) and /NET0026 (J3/J9 pin 21). Similarly, R8 and R22 are both 0 Ω and both connect to /NET0027; their other ends go to /NET0030 (J3/J9 pin 22) and /NET0032 (J3/J9 pin 20).",
      "expected": "For a given M5Stack core variant only one of the two alternative bus pins per PWM channel should be connected. The spec says the jumper set selects pin 19/21 for channel 1 and pin 20/22 for channel 2, with the note 'Short R10, R10 for Core2 and CoreS3 / Short R9, R11 for others', so the unused alternative should be open, not populated.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "spec",
          "quote": "R9–R12 | 0 Ω (jumpers) | Select which M5Stack bus pin (pin 19/21 for ch.1, pin 20/22 for ch.2) supplies PWM1/PWM2 — schematic note: \"Short R10, R10 for Core2 and CoreS3 / Short R9, R11 for others\""
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"14\") (name \"/NET0019\") (class \"Default\")\n      (node (ref \"R16\") (pin \"2\") (pintype \"passive\"))\n      (node (ref \"R20\") (pin \"1\") (pintype \"passive\"))\n      (node (ref \"R7\") (pin \"1\") (pintype \"passive\")))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"7\") (name \"/NET0009\") (class \"Default\")\n      (node (ref \"J3\") (pin \"19\") (pinfunction \"Pin_19\") (pintype \"passive\"))\n      (node (ref \"J9\") (pin \"19\") (pinfunction \"Pin_19\") (pintype \"passive\"))\n      (node (ref \"R7\") (pin \"2\") (pintype \"passive\")))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"19\") (name \"/NET0026\") (class \"Default\")\n      (node (ref \"J3\") (pin \"21\") (pinfunction \"Pin_21\") (pintype \"passive\"))\n      (node (ref \"J9\") (pin \"21\") (pinfunction \"Pin_21\") (pintype \"passive\"))\n      (node (ref \"R20\") (pin \"2\") (pintype \"passive\")))"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "This permanently shorts M5Stack bus pins 19 and 21 together, and pins 20 and 22 together. If either pin is driven by the M5Stack or a stacked module, the two outputs contend, potentially causing malfunction or damage. It also defeats the intended per-core PWM pin selection and, because the serial-mode jumpers are also populated, ties the shared serial servo bus to these PWM GPIO nets through the 1 kΩ series resistors.",
      "confidence": 0.92
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The design files show both alternative PWM bus-select jumpers populated on each channel, shorting M5Stack bus pins 19-21 and 20-22 together contrary to the spec's mutually exclusive jumper selection."
}

